You are working on a Blazor Web App for logistics shipment tracking. The project has been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-ab42506286134fe8a5b51b61b217e4d8/ShipmentTracker/` with:
- `dotnet new blazor -o ShipmentTracker -int Auto -ai -au Individual`
- Interactive Auto, Global mode
- Individual accounts authentication (ASP.NET Core Identity with SQLite)

The solution has two projects:
- `ShipmentTracker/` (server) - hosts the app, API endpoints, EF Core, Identity
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` (WebAssembly) - all interactive UI components

**CRITICAL Auto mode rules:**
- All interactive components/pages go in `.Client` project
- No direct DbContext/server-only access from `.Client` components
- Data access via interface + two implementations (HttpClient in .Client, EF Core in server)
- Both Program.cs must register matching services
- Don't add `@rendermode` to pages (global mode already configured in App.razor)
- Don't add `@rendermode` to Identity/Account pages

## Requirements

Build a shipment tracking app with:
1. **Dispatchers** view a list of shipments with status and destination, can create/update shipments
2. **Customers** check their shipment status and estimated delivery by tracking number
3. Role-based authorization: "Dispatcher" and "Customer" roles
4. Every page has interactive controls

## Implementation Plan

### 1. Shared Data Model (in .Client project so both projects can use it)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Status { get; set; } = "Pending";
    public DateTime CreatedAtUtc { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDeliveryUtc { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDeliveryUtc { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public double? WeightKg { get; set; }
}

public class CreateShipmentDto
{
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public double? WeightKg { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDeliveryUtc { get; set; }
}

public class UpdateShipmentStatusDto
{
    public string Status { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public static class ShipmentStatuses
{
    public const string Pending = "Pending";
    public const string PickedUp = "Picked Up";
    public const string InTransit = "In Transit";
    public const string OutForDelivery = "Out for Delivery";
    public const string Delivered = "Delivered";
    public const string Cancelled = "Cancelled";

    public static readonly string[] All = [Pending, PickedUp, InTransit, OutForDelivery, Delivered, Cancelled];
}
```

### 2. Service Interface (in .Client project)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetShipmentsForCustomerAsync(string email);
    Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(CreateShipmentDto dto);
    Task<ShipmentDto?> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, UpdateShipmentStatusDto dto);
}
```

### 3. Client-side Implementation (in .Client project)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ClientShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ClientShipmentService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{Uri.EscapeDataString(trackingNumber)}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetShipmentsForCustomerAsync(string email)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(email)}") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(CreateShipmentDto dto)
    {
        var response = await http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", dto);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>())!;
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, UpdateShipmentStatusDto dto)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", dto);
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }
}
```

### 4. Server-side Entity and DbContext

Create `ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

